> I don't know how to do this in the Unix environment. In the VMS environment,
> we found that our clients, who had Restricted and Captive accounts, could FTP
> into our machine and see anything with world access, despite the Restricted/
> Captive settings on their accounts.
> 
> To get around it, we implemented Anonymous FTP, which allows someone to FTP
> in using the account ANONYMOUS, and restricts them to the ANONYMOUS directory.
