I didn't see anywhere what version of the OS you are running, but in
V4.0 of DU, you can use dxkerneltuner(1) located in /usr/bin/X11 to
graphically change kernel parameters, including 'maxusers'. In 4.0, most
parameters are configurable at boottime, i.e. you needn't rebuild a
kernel to make them take effect. Just set them using dxkerneltuner(1),
then reboot.

You can also save your changes to a file and load them onto another
system using dxkerneltuner(1).

Some parameters are now 'dynamic' and no longer even need a reboot, but
maxusers is not one of them.



