"dbm store returned -1, errno 28, key "whatever" at TRbot line 1232

I figure  28 is ENOSPC No space left on device.

In "man ndbm" is
  [ENOSPC]  [Digital]  An attempt was made to store a key (and its associated
            contents) whose size exceeds the page block size limit as defined
            by PBLKSIZE in /usr/include/ndbm.h.

In ndbm.h is defined 
#ifdef _XOPEN_SOURCE_EXTENDED
#define DBM_PBLKSIZ 1024
#define DBM_DBLKSIZ 4096

        char    dbm_pagbuf[DBM_PBLKSIZ];/* page file block buffer */
        char    dbm_dirbuf[DBM_DBLKSIZ];/* directory file block buffer */
#else /* _OSF_SOURCE */
#define PBLKSIZ 1024
#define DBLKSIZ 4096
        char    dbm_dirbuf[DBLKSIZ];    /* directory file block buffer */
        char    dbm_pagbuf[PBLKSIZ];    /* page file block buffer */
#endif

So Digital have in their wisdom imposed some arbitrary small limit
on record lengths in a dbm database.

Can I just change this value?
Is it feasible to make a custom version of ndbm and link it
with Perl? Should I just install gdbm ?

